{"v": 2, "built": 1794523679, "courses": [{"id": "jobava", "title": "Jobava London", "side": "white", "sub": "1.d4, 2.Nc3 and 3.Bf4: one simple attacking set-up for White against almost everything", "why": "The Jobava London gives you the same first three moves in nearly every game, so you spend your time on plans, not on memorising. The knight on c3 and the bishop on f4 work together against c7, and many Black players at your level have never seen it. Against best play the position is about equal, but you know the plans and they usually don't. You already reach these positions often: in your games 1.d4 d5 is by far Black's most common answer.", "ideas": [{"t": "Same start every time", "text": "Against ...d5 you play d4, Nc3 and Bf4 first, then e3. The bishop comes out before e3 so it is not locked in behind your pawns.", "shapes": ["g:c1-f4", "g:e2-e3"], "fen": null}, {"t": "Nb5 and the c7 square", "text": "The knight jumps to b5 when c7 can only be guarded by the clumsy ...Na6, or when it wins something. After ...Nc6 Black cannot defend c7 with ...c6, so Nb5 is very strong. If Black can answer ...c6 comfortably, do not jump.", "shapes": ["g:c3-b5", "g:b5-c7", "r:c7"], "fen": "r1bqkb1r/ppp1pppp/2n2n2/1N1p4/3P1B2/8/PPP1PPPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq - 5 4"}, {"t": "Against ...e6: jump at once", "text": "When Black plays ...e6 before ...Bf5 or ...c5, play Nb5 right away, before Black gets ...Bd6 or ...Bb4 in comfortably.", "shapes": ["g:c3-b5", "r:c7"], "fen": "rnbqkb1r/ppp2ppp/4pn2/1N1p4/3P1B2/8/PPP1PPPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq - 1 4"}, {"t": "Against ...Bf5: e3 and Bd3", "text": "Offer to trade your light-squared bishop for Black's best piece. After the trade: Nf3, castle short and push e4.", "shapes": ["g:f1-d3", "g:e3-e4"], "fen": null}, {"t": "Against ...c5: e3 and exd4", "text": "Guard d4 with e3. If Black takes on d4, take back with the e-pawn. Take on c5 when Black's dark-squared bishop would have to move twice to win the pawn back.", "shapes": ["g:e3-d4"], "fen": null}, {"t": "Against an early ...Bb4: Qd3", "text": "The queen on d3 breaks the pin on your knight, guards e4 and b5, and prepares a3 and castling long.", "shapes": ["g:d1-d3", "r:b4"], "fen": null}, {"t": "No pawn on d5? Take the centre", "text": "If Black does not put a pawn on d5 (King's Indian, Pirc, Modern, ...b6), grab the whole centre with e4. Then Bf4, Qd2, castle long and attack with Bh6 and the h-pawn.", "shapes": ["g:e2-e4", "g:c1-h6", "g:h2-h4"], "fen": null}, {"t": "Middlegame plans", "text": "1. A knight on e5 supported by the f-pawn. 2. The e3-e4 pawn break once your pieces are out. 3. The bishop pair after Nxd6. 4. Castle long and push pawns against a fianchetto king.", "shapes": ["g:f3-e5", "g:e3-e4"], "fen": null}], "structures": [{"id": "carlsbad-rev", "t": "Black took on d4: pawns c3 and d4", "fen": "r2qkb1r/1p1b1ppp/p1n1pn2/3pN3/3P1B2/2P5/PP2NPPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq - 0 9", "text": "After ...cxd4 exd4 your d4 pawn is backed up by c3 and cannot be attacked by a Black pawn. The e5 square is yours: put a knight there, guarded by the bishop on f4. Black has the half-open c-file (no pawn of Black's on it) and will try to attack along it. Your plan is to castle, keep the knight on e5 and use the e-file.", "shapes": ["g:f3-e5", "g:c3-d4"]}, {"id": "f4-clamp", "t": "Black took the bishop on f4: pawns d4 and f4", "fen": "rnbq1rk1/ppp2ppp/4pn2/3p4/3P1P2/2NB1N2/PPP2PPP/R2QK2R b KQ - 4 7", "text": "When Black swaps bishops on f4 and you take back with the e-pawn, the pawns on d4 and f4 make e5 a perfect home for your knight: no Black pawn can chase it. Black no longer has a dark-squared bishop, so the dark squares around Black's king are thin. Plan: castle, Ne5, then Qf3 or Qe2 and a rook to the e-file.", "shapes": ["g:f3-e5", "g:f4-e5"]}, {"id": "big-centre", "t": "Pawns on d4 and e4 against a fianchetto", "fen": "rnbq1rk1/ppp1ppbp/3p1np1/8/3PPB2/2N5/PPPQ1PPP/2KR1BNR b - - 5 6", "text": "Against the King's Indian set-up you own the centre with two pawns. The kings are on opposite sides, so both sides attack. Yours is faster: Bh6 swaps off Black's best defender, then the h-pawn runs to h5 to open the h-file.", "shapes": ["g:f4-h6", "g:h2-h5"]}, {"id": "stonewall", "t": "Black's Dutch Stonewall: pawns d5, e6 and f5", "fen": "rnbqkb1r/ppp3pp/4pn2/3p1p2/3P1B2/2N1P3/PPP2PPP/R2QKBNR w KQkq - 0 5", "text": "Black's pawns on d5, e6 and f5 leave a big hole on e5. Your bishop on f4 already controls it and a knight will land there. Black's light-squared bishop is stuck behind its own pawns.", "shapes": ["g:f4-e5", "r:e5"]}, {"id": "symmetrical", "t": "The light bishops are gone: d4 against d5", "fen": "rn1qkb1r/ppp2ppp/4pn2/3p4/3P1B2/2NQP3/PPP2PPP/R3K1NR b KQkq - 0 6", "text": "After Bd3 and the swap of light-squared bishops the centre is level. Your queen on d3 eyes the light squares, your bishop on f4 is still active, and your plan is Nf3, castle short and push e3-e4 to open the game.", "shapes": ["g:e3-e4", "g:d3-h7"]}], "chapters": [{"id": "c5", "title": "Black hits the centre: 3...c5", "intro": "Black attacks your d4 pawn at once. The rule: play e3 first, and if Black takes on d4, take back with the e-pawn. Then develop quickly and use the e5 square.", "lines": ["c5-main", "c5-bg4", "c5-e6"]}], "lines": [{"id": "c5-main", "ch": "c5", "title": "Main line: 4...cxd4 5.exd4 a6", "intro": "Black's most accurate set-up: take on d4 and stop your knight with ...a6. The game is equal, but your plan is easy: Ne5, then a rock-solid pawn chain c3-d4 and a strong knight on d4.", "kind": "main", "nodes": ["58fa55b0", "b8da2df5", "18ce2c61", "77c0ec59", "bc221b5a", "1aa10c23", "8653cbd4", "9d719b9a", "d0b6115c", "6e41e36c", "ce7c58cb", "fc6d4c6d", "6a239bf2", "1bf23823", "fdd61136", "4f41191a", "f27b1afe", "fdcc739c", "f01f16a9", "c62df45c", "9c7d2155", "f02fc3d6", "7522caaa"], "to": null, "reach": 0.00999, "ev": null}, {"id": "c5-bg4", "ch": "c5", "title": "6...Bg4: the bishop for the knight", "intro": "Black pins your knight instead of playing ...Nc6. Kick the bishop with h3; after Black takes on f3 you have the two bishops and a queen ready for a kingside attack.", "kind": "side", "nodes": ["58fa55b0", "b8da2df5", "18ce2c61", "77c0ec59", "bc221b5a", "1aa10c23", "8653cbd4", "9d719b9a", "d0b6115c", "6e41e36c", "ce7c58cb", "c33b3ecb", "fb8cba6a", "19b6a760", "73622f09", "f2c78b7f", "53d841b8", "61467275", "fdd22d9c", "0c819381", "e6ac4fbf", "72cef133", "0fc3147d"], "to": null, "reach": 0.0018, "ev": null}, {"id": "c5-e6", "ch": "c5", "title": "4...e6: the Nb5 jump", "intro": "Black plays ...e6 and ...c5. Your knight jumps to b5 at once and hits c7, so Black must put a knight on the poor a6 square. (The same position comes from 3...e6 4.Nb5 Na6 5.e3 c5.)", "kind": "main", "nodes": ["58fa55b0", "b8da2df5", "18ce2c61", "77c0ec59", "bc221b5a", "1aa10c23", "8653cbd4", "f136ab63", "22024ef6", "b1283858", "ed7a7b1d", "027175d1", "f34331d2", "1639022c", "61f253d6", "4dbe4739", "3c28c745", "4e1d893e", "485d3789"], "to": null, "reach": 0.00265, "ev": null}], "nodes": {"58fa55b0": {"k": "rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq -", "san": "d4", "uci": "d2d4", "ply": 1, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Take the centre with a pawn and open a road for the bishop on c1.", "shapes": ["g:d2-d4"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 20, "loss": 11, "alts": [{"san": "e4", "loss": 0, "note": ""}, {"san": "Nf3", "loss": 11, "note": ""}]}, "b8da2df5": {"k": "rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/3P4/8/PPP1PPPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq -", "san": "d5", "uci": "d7d5", "ply": 2, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 22, "loss": 9, "st": {"n": 310625379, "share": 0.4953, "score": 0.463}}, "18ce2c61": {"k": "rnbqkbnr/ppp1pppp/8/3p4/3P4/8/PPP1PPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq -", "san": "Nc3", "uci": "b1c3", "ply": 3, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "The Jobava move. The knight eyes b5 and e4, and later it can jump to b5 to hit c7.", "shapes": ["g:c3-b5", "r:c7"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 8, "loss": 16, "alts": [{"san": "c4", "loss": 0, "note": ""}, {"san": "Nf3", "loss": 4, "note": ""}, {"san": "Bf4", "loss": 8, "note": ""}]}, "77c0ec59": {"k": "rnbqkbnr/ppp1pppp/8/3p4/3P4/2N5/PPP1PPPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq -", "san": "Nf6", "uci": "g8f6", "ply": 4, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 0, "loss": 0, "st": {"n": 10582324, "share": 0.4424, "score": 0.488}}, "bc221b5a": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/ppp1pppp/5n2/3p4/3P4/2N5/PPP1PPPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq -", "san": "Bf4", "uci": "c1f4", "ply": 5, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Bring the bishop out before you play e3, so it is not shut in behind your own pawns.", "shapes": ["g:c1-f4"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 2, "loss": 0, "alts": []}, "1aa10c23": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/ppp1pppp/5n2/3p4/3P1B2/2N5/PPP1PPPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq -", "san": "c5", "uci": "c7c5", "ply": 6, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 0, "loss": 0, "st": {"n": 317531, "share": 0.0456, "score": 0.497}}, "8653cbd4": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/2pp4/3P1B2/2N5/PPP1PPPP/R2QKBNR w KQkq -", "san": "e3", "uci": "e2e3", "ply": 7, "mine": true, "key": true, "nag": "!", "c": "Solid first: the e-pawn guards d4, and if Black takes on d4 you can take back with this pawn.", "shapes": ["g:e3-d4"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 0, "loss": 0, "alts": [{"san": "e4", "loss": 4, "note": ""}]}, "9d719b9a": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/2pp4/3P1B2/2N1P3/PPP2PPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq -", "san": "cxd4", "uci": "c5d4", "ply": 8, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 4, "loss": 0, "st": null}, "d0b6115c": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3p4/3p1B2/2N1P3/PPP2PPP/R2QKBNR w KQkq -", "san": "exd4", "uci": "e3d4", "ply": 9, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Take back towards the centre. Now the bishop on f1 is free and the e-file is half open for your rook later.", "shapes": ["g:f1-d3"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 4, "loss": 0, "alts": []}, "6e41e36c": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3p4/3P1B2/2N5/PPP2PPP/R2QKBNR b KQkq -", "san": "a6", "uci": "a7a6", "ply": 10, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Black spends a move to stop your knight jumping to b5.", "shapes": ["r:b5"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 1, "loss": 0, "st": null}, "ce7c58cb": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/1p2pppp/p4n2/3p4/3P1B2/2N5/PPP2PPP/R2QKBNR w KQkq -", "san": "Nf3", "uci": "g1f3", "ply": 11, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Develop and aim at the e5 square.", "shapes": ["g:f3-e5"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": -1, "loss": 0, "alts": [{"san": "h3", "loss": 1, "note": ""}, {"san": "Be2", "loss": 1, "note": ""}]}, "fc6d4c6d": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/1p2pppp/p4n2/3p4/3P1B2/2N2N2/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq -", "san": "Nc6", "uci": "b8c6", "ply": 12, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": -1, "loss": 0, "st": null}, "6a239bf2": {"k": "r1bqkb1r/1p2pppp/p1n2n2/3p4/3P1B2/2N2N2/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq -", "san": "Ne5", "uci": "f3e5", "ply": 13, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "The knight jumps to the best square in the middle. It hits the knight on c6 and the pawn on f7, and your bishop on f4 guards it.", "shapes": ["g:f3-e5", "g:f4-e5"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 0, "loss": 1, "alts": [{"san": "h3", "loss": 0, "note": ""}, {"san": "Qd2", "loss": 8, "note": ""}]}, "1bf23823": {"k": "r1bqkb1r/1p2pppp/p1n2n2/3pN3/3P1B2/2N5/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq -", "san": "Bd7", "uci": "c8d7", "ply": 14, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 2, "loss": 0, "st": null}, "fdd61136": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1bpppp/p1n2n2/3pN3/3P1B2/2N5/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq -", "san": "Ne2", "uci": "c3e2", "ply": 15, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "The knight on c3 has nothing to do now that b5 is covered. It goes round to support d4 from e2 and can later come to g3 or f4.", "shapes": ["g:c3-e2", "g:e2-d4"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 3, "loss": 0, "alts": [{"san": "g3", "loss": 10, "note": ""}, {"san": "Be2", "loss": 10, "note": ""}]}, "4f41191a": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1bpppp/p1n2n2/3pN3/3P1B2/8/PPP1NPPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq -", "san": "e6", "uci": "e7e6", "ply": 16, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 2, "loss": 0, "st": null}, "f27b1afe": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1b1ppp/p1n1pn2/3pN3/3P1B2/8/PPP1NPPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq -", "san": "c3", "uci": "c2c3", "ply": 17, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Now the pawns on c3 and d4 hold each other. Nothing can attack your centre, and the b4 square is taken from Black's pieces.", "shapes": ["g:c3-d4", "r:b4"], "plan": {"text": "The position is equal but easy to play. 1. If Black takes on e5, take back with the d-pawn: it grabs space. 2. Your knight on e2 will find a good square in the centre. 3. Castle short and keep the bishop on f4 guarding e5.", "shapes": ["g:d4-e5", "g:e2-d4"]}, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 7, "loss": 0, "alts": [{"san": "Nc1", "loss": 5, "note": ""}, {"san": "Nxd7", "loss": 6, "note": ""}]}, "fdcc739c": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1b1ppp/p1n1pn2/3pN3/3P1B2/2P5/PP2NPPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq -", "san": "Nxe5", "uci": "c6e5", "ply": 18, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": -2, "loss": 0, "st": null}, "f01f16a9": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1b1ppp/p3pn2/3pn3/3P1B2/2P5/PP2NPPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq -", "san": "dxe5", "uci": "d4e5", "ply": 19, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Take back with the pawn. It gains space and kicks the knight off f6.", "shapes": ["g:d4-e5", "r:f6"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 7, "loss": 0, "alts": [{"san": "Bxe5", "loss": 6, "note": ""}]}, "c62df45c": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1b1ppp/p3pn2/3pP3/5B2/2P5/PP2NPPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq -", "san": "Ne4", "uci": "f6e4", "ply": 20, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 3, "loss": 0, "st": null}, "9c7d2155": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1b1ppp/p3p3/3pP3/4nB2/2P5/PP2NPPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq -", "san": "f3", "uci": "f2f3", "ply": 21, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Kick the knight out of the centre at once.", "shapes": ["g:f3-e4"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 2, "loss": 0, "alts": [{"san": "Nd4", "loss": 2, "note": ""}]}, "f02fc3d6": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1b1ppp/p3p3/3pP3/4nB2/2P2P2/PP2N1PP/R2QKB1R b KQkq -", "san": "Nc5", "uci": "e4c5", "ply": 22, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "", "shapes": [], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 7, "loss": 0, "st": null}, "7522caaa": {"k": "r2qkb1r/1p1b1ppp/p3p3/2npP3/5B2/2P2P2/PP2N1PP/R2QKB1R w KQkq -", "san": "Nd4", "uci": "e2d4", "ply": 23, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "The knight takes the hole on d4. No Black pawn can ever chase it away from there.", "shapes": ["g:e2-d4", "g:d4-e6"], "plan": {"text": "Your plan: 1. Qd2, then Be2 and castle short. 2. If Black hits b2 with the queen from b6, guard it with Rb1. 3. Black will try to break your e5 pawn with ...f6: then open the f-file only when your king is safe.", "shapes": ["g:d1-d2", "g:f4-e5"]}, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 8, "loss": 0, "alts": [{"san": "Qd2", "loss": 5, "note": ""}]}, "c33b3ecb": {"k": "rnbqkb1r/1p2pppp/p4n2/3p4/3P1B2/2N2N2/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R b KQkq -", "san": "Bg4", "uci": "c8g4", "ply": 12, "mine": false, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Black pins the knight to your queen.", "shapes": ["r:g4-d1"], "plan": null, "x": [], "quiz": null, "ev": 9, "loss": 10, "st": null}, "fb8cba6a": {"k": "rn1qkb1r/1p2pppp/p4n2/3p4/3P1Bb1/2N2N2/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq -", "san": "h3", "uci": "h2h3", "ply": 13, "mine": true, "key": false, "nag": null, "c": "Ask the bishop at once: take or go back.", "shapes":